    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0629" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.12/36: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-11T19:00:00+08:00">August 11, 1930—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:38 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>689. Department’s 256, July 31, 6 p.m.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d593-f1"/> Legation
                    has received from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs copies of quarantine
                    regulations with request that those concerned be instructed to comply with the
                    regulations. A reply is being drafted along the lines of the Department’s
                    telegram under reference. Shanghai reported under date of <pb facs="0630"
                        n="532" xml:id="pg532"/> August 7, 1 p.m., similar reply made to Director of
                    Quarantine. Shanghai informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d593-f1" n="34" xml:id="d593-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram of the same date to the Consul General at
                    Shanghai, <ref target="#pg529">p. 529</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
